# ============================================================
# .gitignore for a Stata + LaTeX (+ Python) research project
# Track: code (.do, .py), .tex source, and small look-up tables.
# Ignore: data, logs, build artifacts, and large binaries.
# ============================================================

# ---------- Data (keep raw/large data OUT of git) ----------
# Stata / tabular / binary datasets are usually large and re-createable.
# If you WANT to track a specific file, add an exception, e.g.:
#   !CODE/crosswalks/statefip_lookup.dta
*.dta
*.dtas
*.csv
*.tsv
*.txt
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.parquet
*.feather
*.sas7bdat
*.RData
*.rds
*.json.gz

# Common data folders (adjust names to your layout)
DATA/
data/
RAW/
raw/
raw_data/
output_data/
derived/
build/
extracts/
temp/
tmp/

# ---------- Large media / scraped images & archives ----------
*.zip
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp

# ---------- Stata ----------
# NOTE: gitignore has no inline comments -- a trailing "# ..." becomes part
# of the pattern and the rule silently matches nothing. Keep comments on
# their own line.
# Stata (and LaTeX) logs, formatted logs, autosave/recovery, and graph files
# (the last are regenerated from the .do files).
*.log
*.smcl
*.stswap
*.gph
# ...but the reviewer transcripts under review/reports/ ARE the audit trail and
# are committed on purpose. Ten of them were already tracked when *.log began
# matching; without this exception new ones would be silently left behind.
!review/reports/*.log
sigma.dta
_stata_temp*/

# ---------- LaTeX build artifacts ----------
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.idx
*.ilg
*.ind
*.lof
*.lot
*.nav
*.out
*.run.xml
*.snm
*.synctex.gz
*.synctex(busy)
*.toc
*.vrb
*.xdv
*.brf
*.dvi
*.spl
*.thm
*.acn
*.acr
*.alg
*.glg
*.glo
*.gls
*.ist
# Keep the compiled paper by default. To ignore built PDFs instead,
# delete the two lines below and uncomment "*.pdf".
# *.pdf
!*.pdf

# ---------- Python ----------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.env

# ---------- Editors / OS ----------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------- Claude / Cowork ----------
# Share team settings (.claude/settings.json) but keep personal overrides local.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
